   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"><b><em style="font: inherit;">10.</em> EMPLOYEE BENEFIT PLAN</b></p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">Employees of the Company <em style="font: inherit;"> may </em>participate in the Zevia LLC <em style="font: inherit;">401</em>(k) Plan (the &#8220;Plan&#8221;), a defined contribution plan which qualifies under Section <em style="font: inherit;">401</em>(k) of the Internal Revenue Code. Participating employees <em style="font: inherit;"> may </em>contribute from <em style="font: inherit;">1%</em> to <em style="font: inherit;">90%</em> of their pre-tax earnings, up to the statutory limit. Effective <em style="font: inherit;"> January 1, 2020, </em>the Company began offering matching contributions to the Plan of up to <em style="font: inherit;">4%</em> of employee pre-tax earnings. For the years ended <em style="font: inherit;"> December 31, 2025 </em>and <em style="font: inherit;">2024</em>, the Company incurred contribution expense of $<ix:nonFraction id="c140555235" contextRef="d_2025-01-01_2025-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:DefinedContributionPlanCostRecognized" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">0.4</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction id="c140555236" contextRef="d_2024-01-01_2024-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:DefinedContributionPlanCostRecognized" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">0.4</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million, respectively.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;&#160;</p>
